# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HI-MC run outputs and machine-local settings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# focus_map writes one tile plan per region on every run (154 of them had
# accumulated here). They are output, not source. One is kept as an example
# of the format - see the negation below - so the layout can be read without
# having to do a run first.
tile_plan_propagate_tilt_1pt_*.csv
!tile_plan_propagate_tilt_1pt_S10R1.csv

# Same for focus_map's per-region tile list (output_tiles_csv), including
# the ones written for partial retakes. One example kept, same region as
# the tile plan above so the two can be read side by side.
tiles_*.csv
!tiles_S10R1.csv

# Diagnostic plots written by the fit/compare scripts.
expected_vs_measured_ol_*.png

# Who gets failure alerts is per-deployment, and the file holds real email
# addresses. Create your own; alerts.py reads one address per line.
himc_notify_emails.txt

# Claude Code's per-machine tool permissions - absolute paths from one
# workstation, meaningless anywhere else.
.claude/
